# Skill: web-ui

Use this skill when testing, verifying, or automating web browser interactions.

## When to invoke

- Verifying a UI-facing acceptance criterion
- Writing or updating a browser-automation test
- Investigating a visual discrepancy or broken interaction
- Generating screenshot evidence for a ticket

## Tool to use

Use the Playwright MCP connector (or your configured browser automation tool).
Do **not** re-explore the DOM if a test already covers the scenario — check
`.claude/rules/test-execution-path.md` first.

## Evidence rules

For every Given / When / Then step:

1. Take a screenshot **after** inputs are filled/selected, **before** the action
2. Take a follow-up screenshot **after** the action showing the result (success/error/redirect)
3. Every dropdown scenario needs a screenshot per option exercised
4. A passed UI step without a screenshot does not count as verified

## Locator hierarchy (most to least preferred)

```
role / aria-label        → role=button[name="Save"]
data-testid              → [data-testid="submit-btn"]
id                       → #submit-btn
semantic CSS             → button.primary
XPath                    → use only when nothing else works
```

Declare locators as constants at the top of the file — never inline in keywords/steps.

## Strict mode & scope

Scope locators to the active section/panel to avoid ambiguity:

```python
# Playwright (Python)
panel = page.locator('[data-testid="details-panel"]')
panel.get_by_label("Name").fill("Test value")
```

## Cross-browser note

Run dev verification in one browser (Chromium by default). Staging verification should
ideally cover a second browser (Firefox or WebKit) for any UI-facing AC.

## Common gotchas

| Symptom | Likely cause |
|---|---|
| Element not found | Page not loaded, wrong locator, wrong env URL |
| Intermittent failures | Race condition — add an explicit wait for the element |
| Action succeeds but no change | Save button re-enabled on backend rejection — check for error banners |
| Screenshot shows wrong state | Screenshot taken too early — wait for network idle |

## Screenshot evidence naming

```
given-01-<state-description>.png
when-01-<action-description>.png
then-01-<expected-result>.png
```

Store under `evidence/<TICKET-KEY>/<scenario-slug>/`.
